r","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":8,"closed_issues":4466,"state":"closed","created_at":"2024-02-14T11:52:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T23:48:31Z","due_on":"2025-03-03T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-03-19T09:35:35Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-01-27T14:26:24Z","updated_at":"2025-01-28T15:12:09Z","closed_at":"2025-01-28T15:08:58Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible on master (e5498020b6250d9284efcdcf0f85f39d48d8548f)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.beta (e5498020b) - macOS Sequoia (15.2.0) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Apple M3 Max - Apple M3 Max (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nRendering a CurveTexture on standard platforms reveal no issues.\n\n<img width=\"381\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c042e0a8-5e19-46f7-8c24-afeabd33c316\" />\n\nBut rendering a CurveTexture on iOS Safari results in a black image.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/364a0cee-001e-4077-9906-2a7ed77903a6)\n\nI printed the contents of the texture data, and it doesn't seem awry. Later testing revealed that it's an image format issue.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a TextureRect. (and ideally set a minimal size like 300x300)\n2. Use a CurveTexture inside it.\n3. Setup the curve of that curve texture until you have a black and white texture\n4. Test on the desktop, see that the image is displayed\n5. Test on an iPad, see that the image is black\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[curve_texture_test_2025-01-27_09-23-32.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18559398/curve_texture_test_2025-01-27_09-23-32.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6V